      {
        "id": 87103,
        "name": "Sefirit",
        "username": "Sefirit",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e68b1a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-21T17:06:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"grysqrl\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/grysqrl/48/1909_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> grysqrl:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Not quite:</p>\n<div><b>Sefirit wrote:</b><br><blockquote>IF ((Not(played a card<s> in your play phase</s>)AND(Not(used a power<s> in your power phase</s>))) THEN you may draw an additional card during the draw phase.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>While I agree that is the correct conversion for what arenson9 wrote, the \"in your X phase\" parts fit with what Foote initially stated.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Foote wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Skipping your turn does not give you an extra card draw. Skipping your turn is not a option the game gives to you.If you do not play a card in your play phase or use a power in your power phase, you may draw 2 cards during the draw phase.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;If I may, a minor, friendly correction: If you neither play a card nor use a power you may draw an additional card during the draw phase.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I also believe that is the correct interpretaion of the rule according to jagarciao:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jagarciao\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/48/2010_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jagarciao:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As Foote pointed out, in order to draw that extra card in your Draw phase, what you actually did was you opted not to play a card during your Play phase and then opted not to use a power during your Power phase.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This means that if Omni-X has out a component that lets him play a card during the start of his turn and he does, then does not play a card during the play phase and also refrains from using a power during his power phase he will get the extra card draw.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:11:17.283Z",
