        "id": 87105,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-21T19:45:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><b>Rabit wrote:</b><br>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><blockquote>Yeah, the wording on page 6&nbsp;of <a href=\"http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/system/files/downloads/Sentinels%20of%20the%20Multiverse%20Enhanced%20Edition%20Rulebook.pdf\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">the rule book</a> (page 9 of the PDF) is pretty specific: \"If, for any reason, a player neither plays a card nor uses a power on their turn, then they may draw an additional card during their draw phase. If, by contrast, a player skips their turn for any reason, they have skipped every phase of their turn and cannot draw any cards.\"\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thanks, Pydro - beat me to it.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/innocent.png?v=12\" title=\":innocent:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":innocent:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
